---
description: What must never reach a tracked file, a commit or a pull request
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository is public. The working session that produces the work is not, and the
boundary is one way. Never write a named competitor or their products, docs, pricing or
behaviour; growth, marketing or business strategy; or anything said in a session that is
not a technical requirement — into a tracked file, a commit message, a pull request, an
issue or a code comment.

Reference material shared during development is for reading, not for keeping. Take the
requirement out of it, state the requirement in the product's own words, and let the
reference go.

The full rule, and everything else that governs work here, is in `AGENTS.md`. Read it.
`python3 Scripts/disclosure_audit.py` enforces this and runs in `make verify`, in the
pre-push and commit-msg hooks, and on every pull request.
